{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "John Denver and Peter, Paul and Mary feel like natural next choices because their melodic folk songs and harmonies connect with my listening to Jonathan Edwards, Melanie, and Simon & Garfunkel.",
    "Seals & Crofts fits the mellow, familiar songs I want now, while Clapton and Billy Squier make sense alongside the classic rock in my history."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The 20/20 Experience does not fit my current interest in older folk and classic rock collections; my past interest in Born This Way does not mean I want more contemporary pop today.",
    "The comedy album does not serve my interest in music, and titles like Ultimate Collection, x, and Greatest Hits Of All, The give me too little evidence of a musical match to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits or collection title alone is not enough for me; the artist and the sound are what make a collection appealing.",
    "My listening spans pop and rock, but treating all of those past choices as equally relevant misses my preference for gentler songs today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Melanie, Jonathan Edwards, and Simon & Garfunkel points toward melodic folk and vocal harmonies, which matter more to me right now than a broad connection to rock.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose today: Clapton and Billy Squier interest me, but the folk collections are stronger immediate choices."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understand my interest in older music collections, but miss how strongly melodic folk and gentler songs guide my choices right now."
}"}
